# Brainana example dataset

A small, ready-to-run BIDS dataset used to demo the Brainana macaque MRI
preprocessing pipeline. It contains a single subject and session:

    sub-example/ses-001/
    ├── anat/
    │   ├── sub-example_ses-001_run-1_T1w.nii.gz   (+ .json)
    │   ├── sub-example_ses-001_run-2_T1w.nii.gz   (+ .json)
    │   └── sub-example_ses-001_run-1_T2w.nii.gz   (+ .json)
    └── func/
        ├── sub-example_ses-001_task-rest_run-1_bold.nii.gz   (+ .json)
        └── sub-example_ses-001_task-rest_run-2_bold.nii.gz   (+ .json)

Two anatomical T1w runs (plus a T2w) exercise Brainana's multi-run anatomical
selection; two resting-state functional runs exercise the functional workflow.

Data are acquired on a Siemens Prisma 3T scanner. Site- and scanner-identifying
metadata fields (institution name/address, device serial number, station name)
have been removed from the JSON sidecars; acquisition parameters needed by the
pipeline (repetition/echo time, slice timing, phase-encoding direction, etc.)
are retained.

How to run this dataset through Brainana is documented under "Example dataset
(demo)" in the Usage notes:
https://brainana.readthedocs.io/en/stable/usage_notes.html
